WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.840
Pakistan's airstrikes on Afghan civilian areas have killed three people and raised the risk of renewed border fighting between the two neighbors. This is Omni View, episode 182. This briefing puts the facts first, then the named governments and newsrooms that disagree about what those facts mean. Where a story has no genuine dispute, a signed deal, a market test, a death, you will hear context, and what is being done next, not a manufactured argument.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:34.780
The dead were members of one family. Bloomberg and the Hindu report those casualty figures

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:39.820
from Taliban sources, and both note there has been no independent confirmation from

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:45.420
the ground. The strikes came days after an assault on a police facility inside Pakistan,

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:52.080
an attack Islamabad has linked to Afghan officials. An air strike happened. The live disagreement

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:57.860
is whether the target was a legitimate security site or a civilian home. The Taliban described

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:02.480
the strike as hitting civilian targets, and warned it could spark wider clashes.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:06.000
In that account, this was not a raid on a militant camp.

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:10.980
It was a family in a civilian area, and the next step could be fighting along the border,

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:12.740
rather than a one-eaf operation.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:17.720
Pakistani officials have not issued a public statement on this specific incident.

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:23.180
They have previously said that cross-border militant activity justifies defensive action.

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:27.840
That is the justification they have offered for this kind of operation in the past.

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:33.780
Militants moving across the border, a police facility attacked at home, and a duty to respond.

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:38.900
Even that argument, as they have made it, has not yet been applied by them in public

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:40.220
to this particular strike.

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:44.220
So the shared record is an air strike and a family among the dead.

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:48.700
The split is over what was hit and who owes the public an account of it.

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:54.040
The United States' virtual embassy in Iran has issued a security alert telling American

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:55.640
citizens to leave the country.

00:01:56.160 --> 00:02:01.360
The notice, reported by the Hindu, cited a complex security environment and warned of

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:06.340
possible flight cancellations, airspace closures, and other travel disruptions.

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:12.140
Washington's own reading is that risks across West Asia are increasing, and that Americans

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:16.180
still in Iran should not wait to find out whether commercial routes stay open.

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:20.800
The Iranian state media have not directly addressed the United States warning.

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:26.300
They continue to frame regional tensions as driven by external actors, which puts the

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:31.020
cause of the danger outside Iran rather than inside the country's own security picture.

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:36.940
The Hindu places the advisory in the longer one of the United States' Iran friction, and

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:41.040
it does not add fresh on-the-ground verification of conditions for travelers.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:47.080
The practical contents of the alert are specific, depart, and plan for the possibility that

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:49.060
flights stop and airspace closes.

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:54.400
What happens next depends on whether those travel disruptions actually appear, and on

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:59.180
whether Tehran answers the warning in public or leaves the American notice unanswered.

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:05.440
Preliminary results from Russia's parliamentary election indicate that United Russia, the Kremlin

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:08.940
backed party, is on course to keep its constitutional majority.

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:14.500
International observers have described the outcome as holding no surprises, and BBC

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:17.680
World News notes the continuity with previous votes.

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:22.860
Russian state outlets present the same strong result as a clear endorsement of the current

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:23.320
leadership.

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:29.140
The factual baseline accepted across those reports is that United Russia performed strongly.

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:33.940
Everything in the coverage turns on how a lopsided result is supposed to be read.

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:38.860
The strongest case Russian state outlets make is that voters have again chosen the

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:43.680
governing party, and that the constitutional majority is a mandate, not a formality.

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:49.160
BBC World News and the observers who said there were no surprises are describing something

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:54.420
quieter, a result that looks like the last one in a contest that did not scramble the map.

00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:58.060
Preliminary counts are still the basis for all of this.

00:03:58.580 --> 00:04:00.820
The party is on course to retain the majority.

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:04.860
The final seeding of that majority is what the count still has to finish.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:10.380
The United States President Donald Trump and French President Emmanuel Macron will hold

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:11.940
talks in New York on Monday.

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:17.560
Both leaders are attending the United Nations or UN General Assembly session this week,

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:18.660
the White House said.

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:22.500
The White House confirmed the meeting without detailing an agenda.

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:27.960
French officials have indicated they expect discussion of European security and Middle East

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:28.500
developments.

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:34.480
France 24 reports the encounter as part of routine diplomatic scheduling before the larger

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:40.880
assembly, not as a sudden crisis summit. So the facts on the calendar are plain. Two presidents,

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:47.380
one city, one day, and a UN week around them. Paris has named the subjects it expects.

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:53.720
Washington has not named subjects at all. What happens next is the meeting itself and whether

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:59.740
either capital then describes what was actually discussed. Vietnam has been added to the financial

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:06.260
time stock exchange, or FTSE, emerging market index. The change is expected to draw additional

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:11.660
foreign capital into Vietnamese stocks and bonds, and coverage of the move has spoken of billions

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:18.380
in possible inflows. Nique Asia reports that index inclusion typically triggers automatic purchases

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:23.860
by funds that track the benchmark. Vietnamese authorities have welcomed the move as recognition

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:29.960
of market reforms. The factual step is the reclassification itself. The scale of those

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:34.820
inflows remains to be measured in the coming quarters. The platform is intended to support

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:40.880
greater foreign participation in local markets, with that wider access set to be implemented next year.

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:46.080
Bloomberg notes the test is part of efforts to modernize financial infrastructure.

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:51.360
Market participants expect the change to reduce settlement risk for international investors

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:55.800
who now have to work around a market that stops when Seoul's business day stops.

00:05:56.260 --> 00:06:02.340
The central bank has stated the system will run in parallel with existing daytime operations during the trial phase,

00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:05.540
so the old rails stay up while the new ones are checked.

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:10.260
President William Ruto witnessed a signing that his progress worth knowing.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:17.080
Kenya, the United Nations, and Equity Group agreed to deepen how Kenyans abroad take part in the country's development.

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:23.840
The pact aims to increase diaspora participation through investment, skills transfer, and enterprise

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:30.260
creation. All Africa reports it as a concrete step to channel remittances and expertise into

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:35.620
domestic projects rather than leaving that money and know how only in private family channels.

00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:41.540
The main complication noted is that past diaspora initiatives have faced delays in regulatory

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:48.240
approval and in trust building. The number of participating diaspora members and the volume of funds

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:54.220
mobilized will be tracked in the coming months. To really understand how index inclusion channels

00:06:54.220 --> 00:07:00.140
foreign money start with the misunderstanding most headlines invite that a country joining a major

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:06.260
stock index automatically receives a flood of cash. In practice, the mechanism runs through passive

00:07:06.260 --> 00:07:12.060
of funds, funds that copy an index rather than picking winners by hand. Those funds must

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:16.580
buy the new constituents in proportion to their waiting once the reclassification takes

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:22.700
effect. The purchases are mechanical rather than discretionary, which is why the size of inflows

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:28.060
can be estimated from the amount of assets tracking that particular index. The same rules

00:07:28.060 --> 00:07:32.780
create selling pressure later if a country is removed because the tracker has to dump

00:07:32.780 --> 00:07:39.520
what the index no longer lists. The reclassification decision itself rests on measurable thresholds for

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:45.420
market size, liquidity, and accessibility, and the footsie reviews those on a fixed schedule.

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:50.680
Vietnam's addition followed sustained policy steps to open capital markets,

00:07:51.040 --> 00:07:55.160
including adjustments to foreign ownership limits that met the benchmark standards.

00:07:55.760 --> 00:07:59.100
When you hear a claim that inclusion will transform an economy,

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:05.960
The check is the actual size of the passive funds involved, and whether active investors are following the same path.

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:12.260
Cross-check the announcement against the index provider's own papers, not against a single news summary.

00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:22.380
Primary documents such as methodology papers and central bank notices in other market stories often contain the precise conditions that later reporting simplifies.

00:08:22.380 --> 00:08:27.740
Next time an index announcement appears, open that methodology document and look for

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:32.520
the rebalancing schedule and the minimum free float requirement that decided eligibility.

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:38.820
If you want to go deeper on the Pakistan-Afghanistan strikes, compare how Bloomberg and the Hindu

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:39.640
are covering them.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:45.280
You will see two different frames on the same casualty figures and the same gap in independent

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:45.900
confirmation.

00:08:46.660 --> 00:08:51.260
Tomorrow, watch for whether the White House or French officials describe what was actually

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:56.060
said in New York, including any language on European security or the Middle East.

